{
  "reasoning": "The lecture continues the VR software discussion by completing the virtual-world-generator components with physics and networked collaboration, then compares developer options, game engines, and deployment options. I merged the opening/recap into the first physics segment because opening remarks must not stand alone, and I cut at clear bridges such as 41, 60, 102, 119, 163, 174, 194, and 219. For the game-engine examples, I moved the cut from 146 to 148 so the examples segment does not depend on the phrase 'these components' from the previous segment, while 146-147 still close the sub-engine discussion. The final segment is a closing summary/preview segment.",
